---
import PapersExplorer from '../../components/PapersExplorer.astro';
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { getPapers } from '../../lib/papers';

const papers = await getPapers();
const counts = {
  queued: papers.filter((paper) => paper.data.progress === 'queued').length,
  skimmed: papers.filter((paper) => paper.data.progress === 'skimmed').length,
  read: papers.filter((paper) => paper.data.progress === 'read').length,
};
---

<PageLayout
  title="Reading list"
  eyebrow="Editorial triage cockpit"
  lead="The editorial triage cockpit for scanned computational genomics candidates. Expand full abstracts, select ✨ Deep Dive to prioritize papers for two-gate synthesis or 🗑️ Archive to discard, and export decision batches. Reading progress reflects editorial workflow status, not intrinsic scientific merit."
>
  <dl class="progress-summary">
    <div class="progress-summary__item">
      <div class="progress-summary__meta">
        <dt>Queued</dt>
        <span class="progress-summary__hint">Candidates to triage</span>
      </div>
      <dd>{counts.queued}</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="progress-summary__item">
      <div class="progress-summary__meta">
        <dt>Skimmed</dt>
        <span class="progress-summary__hint">Active & triaged</span>
      </div>
      <dd>{counts.skimmed}</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="progress-summary__item">
      <div class="progress-summary__meta">
        <dt>Read</dt>
        <span class="progress-summary__hint">Full synthesis published</span>
      </div>
      <dd>{counts.read}</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <section class="triage-guide" aria-label="Candidate triage instructions">
    <div class="triage-guide__header">
      <p class="triage-guide__eyebrow">Editorial Workflow</p>
      <h2>Candidate Triage & Editorial Dispatch</h2>
      <p class="triage-guide__intro">
        Scanned preprints enter this queue awaiting human curation. Follow this three-step workflow to triage candidates and trigger automated deep dives:
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="triage-steps">
      <li class="triage-step">
        <div class="triage-step__marker" aria-hidden="true">1</div>
        <div class="triage-step__body">
          <h3>Expand full abstracts</h3>
          <p>Click <strong>Abstract</strong> on individual paper cards or use the top <strong>Expand All Abstracts</strong> button to review architectures, datasets, and benchmarks without leaving the list.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="triage-step">
        <div class="triage-step__marker" aria-hidden="true">2</div>
        <div class="triage-step__body">
          <h3>Mark candidate decisions</h3>
          <p>Select <strong class="triage-step__highlight--accent">✨ Deep Dive</strong> to flag papers for comprehensive technical synthesis, or <strong class="triage-step__highlight--archive">🗑️ Archive</strong> to discard non-target candidates.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="triage-step">
        <div class="triage-step__marker" aria-hidden="true">3</div>
        <div class="triage-step__body">
          <h3>Export & dispatch via drawer</h3>
          <p>Use the floating bottom action drawer to <strong>Copy CLI Commands</strong> (<code>gh workflow run summarize.yml ...</code>) for batch pipeline dispatch, or export decisions as structured JSON.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="survey-briefing" aria-labelledby="survey-briefing-title">
    <div class="survey-briefing__header">
      <p class="survey-briefing__eyebrow">Daily Survey Briefing · Sep 3, 2026</p>
      <h2 id="survey-briefing-title">Today's Survey: 13 Papers on Genomic Foundation Models, Context Compression & Single-Cell Scaling</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="survey-briefing__content">
      <p class="survey-briefing__lead">
        Today's literature survey captures 13 newly queued papers spanning model compression, verifiable interpretability, evolutionary tokenization, and single-cell scaling. Below is the technical synthesis of today's key breakthroughs and methodologies:
      </p>

      <div class="survey-themes">
        <article class="theme-card">
          <div class="theme-card__tag">Inference & Serving</div>
          <h3>Extreme Context Compression (Evo 2)</h3>
          <p>
            <strong>TurboQuant-Bio</strong> (<a href="/papers/calibration-free-compression-brings-evo-2-to-its-full-million-token-context-on-a-single-gpu-75592d4/">Patsakis et al.</a>) achieves near-lossless 4-bit compression of Evo 2 weights and attention cache without calibration data. It serves both through fused custom kernels, bringing Evo 2 40B onto one 80 GB GPU and Evo 2 7B to its full 1,000,000-token context within 40 GB memory—an 8× context gain. It also discovers that the released chunked-prefill path silently produces uncorrelated likelihoods and repairs it, enabling a 580 kb bacterial genome to be scored in 22 minutes rather than 13.7 hours.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="theme-card">
          <div class="theme-card__tag">Interpretability & Verification</div>
          <h3>Verifiable Sequence-to-Function</h3>
          <p>
            <strong>S2F-Agent</strong> (<a href="/papers/s2f-agent-harnessing-sequence-to-function-models-for-verifiable-genome-interpretation-ad7a239/">Li et al.</a>) shifts genome interpretation from black-box neural scoring to verifiable multi-agent reasoning, orchestrating sequence-to-function foundation models with automated evidence verification. In parallel, <a href="/papers/evaluating-post-hoc-explanations-of-dnabert-2-0d229cf/">Kurth et al.</a> evaluate post-hoc feature attribution on DNABERT-2, identifying baseline selection issues in Integrated Gradients and providing guidelines for faithful biological motif attribution.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="theme-card">
          <div class="theme-card__tag">Architecture & Pretraining</div>
          <h3>Evolution-Guided Tokenization & Multimodal DNA</h3>
          <p>
            <strong>EvoLen</strong> (<a href="/papers/evolen-evolution-guided-tokenization-for-dna-language-model-c8a483f/">Huang et al.</a>) demonstrates that statistical BPE tokenization fragments regulatory motifs, proposing token dictionaries derived from multi-species evolutionary conservation alignments. Complementing this, <a href="/papers/a-self-supervised-dna-foundation-model-with-collapse-resistant-multimodal-fusion-3e53471/">Chen</a> develops a collapse-resistant multimodal fusion mechanism preventing DNA sequence features from dominating chromatin accessibility in joint pretraining.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="theme-card">
          <div class="theme-card__tag">Single-Cell Genomics</div>
          <h3>Scaling Laws & Generative Transcriptomics</h3>
          <p>
            <strong>Scaling recipes for scRNA-seq</strong> (<a href="/papers/scaling-recipes-for-single-cell-rna-sequencing-foundation-models-when-do-scaling-laws-hold-1f1cc71/">Borra et al.</a>) establishes empirical boundaries for when model and data scaling yield real transfer gains in single-cell foundation models. For generative synthesis, <a href="/papers/scaling-an-autoregressive-transformer-for-single-cell-generation-b07d981/">Sharipov et al.</a> scale autoregressive transformers to synthesize realistic multi-gene profiles, while <strong>COBRA</strong> (<a href="/papers/cobra-cell-type-specific-orthogonal-batch-effect-removal-algorithm-54a7f07/">Seo et al.</a>) introduces orthogonal subspace projection to eliminate batch confounders without erasing subtle biological heterogeneity.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="theme-card">
          <div class="theme-card__tag">Structural & Spatial Omics</div>
          <h3>3D Chromatin Connectomes & RNA Therapeutics</h3>
          <p>
            <a href="/papers/3d-epigenome-of-glial-cell-types-in-developing-human-cortex-2307d51/">Jones et al. (Nature)</a> map high-resolution 3D chromatin loops across glial lineages in the developing human cortex, physically linking non-coding neuropsychiatric risk variants to target promoters. On the molecular side, <strong>GRASSP</strong> (<a href="/papers/grassp-rna-language-model-enhanced-graph-attention-cf1011e/">Nguyen & Le</a>) pairs RNA language models with adaptive gated graph attention to predict small-molecule binding sites on structured RNA targets, and <strong>Yanez Sarmiento et al.</strong> (<a href="/papers/interpreting-protein-language-model-embeddings-via-orthogonal-projection-5a308a6/">arXiv:2608.25548</a>) use orthogonal projection on PLM embeddings for zero-shot protein fitness prediction.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <PapersExplorer papers={papers} action="/reading-list/" defaultProgress="queued" />
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .progress-summary {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .progress-summary__item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.15rem clamp(1rem, 2.5vw, 1.75rem);
    transition: background 0.15s ease;
  }

  .progress-summary__item:hover {
    background: var(--color-surface-hover);
  }

  .progress-summary__item + .progress-summary__item {
    border-left: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .progress-summary__meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.2rem;
  }

  .progress-summary dt {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .progress-summary__hint {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    font-weight: 450;
  }

  .progress-summary dd {
    color: var(--color-accent-strong);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
    font-weight: 650;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  /* Triage Guide Section */
  .triage-guide {
    margin-top: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem);
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  }

  .triage-guide__eyebrow {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .triage-guide__header h2 {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .triage-guide__intro {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .triage-steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 18rem), 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.35rem;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .triage-step {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    background: var(--color-surface-muted);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    transition: border-color 0.15s ease, background 0.15s ease;
  }

  .triage-step:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-rule-strong);
    background: var(--color-surface-hover);
  }

  .triage-step__marker {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 1.75rem;
    height: 1.75rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-on-accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .triage-step__body h3 {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .triage-step__body p {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    font-size: var(--fs-abstract);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }

  .triage-step__body code {
    padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }

  .triage-step__highlight--accent {
    color: var(--color-accent-strong);
  }

  .triage-step__highlight--archive {
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  /* Daily Survey Briefing */
  .survey-briefing {
    margin-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.25rem);
    padding: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    background: var(--color-surface-muted);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  }

  .survey-briefing__eyebrow {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .survey-briefing__header h2 {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.2vw, 1.75rem);
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .survey-briefing__lead {
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .survey-themes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 19rem), 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }

  .theme-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.35rem;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
    transition: border-color 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;
  }

  .theme-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-rule-strong);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
  }

  .theme-card__tag {
    align-self: flex-start;
    padding: 0.22rem 0.6rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: var(--color-surface-muted);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .theme-card h3 {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.32;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .theme-card p {
    margin-top: 0.65rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--fs-abstract);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .theme-card a {
    color: var(--color-accent-strong);
    font-weight: 550;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .progress-summary {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .progress-summary__item + .progress-summary__item {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
      border-left: 0;
    }

    .triage-step {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }

    .theme-card {
      padding: 1.1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
